          "english_quote": "to whom it was fitting that these visions should be revealed",
          "issue": "The rendering reduces the obligation expressed by ἔδει to fitness or appropriateness. The lexical rationale explicitly acknowledges choosing wording softer than necessity, but supplies no passage-specific evidence warranting that reduction. The clause says these visions ought to have been revealed to the other, prior and better people; it does not merely describe them as suitable recipients.",
          "suggested_revision": "Consider “to whom these visions ought to have been revealed,” and revise the ἔδει lexical decision accordingly. This proposed replacement requires fresh review before acceptance.",
          "severity": "major"
        }
